From 5e1bcaea8b59a2e78b0b36257f4f2b1ecc3af26c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rico Rojas <rickrojas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:59:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dictation): remove filler words before cleanup or paste

A toggle (default on) and an editable word list, the same shape Fluid
Voice offers: um, uh, er, ah, eh, umm, uhh, err, ahh, ehh, hmm, hm, mm,
mmm, erm, urm, ugh. Pure string work in the renderer right after the
transcript arrives, so it costs nothing and the cleanup model never sees
the fillers. Whisper large-v3-turbo drops most fillers on its own but
not all (four clips re-run raw on 2026-09-08: three clean, one kept
"But, uh, does it, um...").

- fillerWords.js: whole-word, Unicode-aware, case-insensitive; absorbs
  the commas and dashes around a filler, keeps a real sentence stop, and
  re-capitalises the word that now opens a sentence
- settingsStore/useSettings: removeFillerWords and fillerWords, persisted
- SettingsPage AI Models: toggle, chips with remove, add field, reset
- audioManager.processTranscriptionCore applies it before reasoning

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015uYKeUK2xoKRQMj5gCikCq
